    "available_at": "2026-11-27T15:43:51.596893+00:00",
    "body": "Great on any Friday: 70mai M800 4K Dash Cam - Front+Rear, Voice Control, Parking Monitor\nAll-New Zeekr 7X Is a 785-Horsepower Electric SUV That Hits 62 MPH in 2.98 Seconds\n10 photos\nPhoto: Zeekr\nZeekr officially unveiled the 7X at the 2026 Guangzhou Auto Show. The model launches with a promotional starting price of roughly $32,000. For the money, customers get the refreshed mid-size electric SUV sitting on a 900-volt architecture, a new battery option, and a hardware upgrade across all trims.\nThe entire Zeekr 7X lineup is now underpinned by the new 900-volt high-voltage platform. A new 85-kWh Energee Golden Brick LFP battery pack joins the 7X lineup, offering 5.5C charging support, recharging from 10% to 8% in roughly 10.5 minutes.\nAt the top of the lineup sits the dual-motor Ultra variant with a dual-motor powertrain, producing 785 horsepower (795 metric horsepower) and 599 pound-feet (812 Newton meters) of torque. That is enough to make it rocket from 0 to 62 mph (0 to 100 kph) in just 2.98 seconds, which basically places the midsize SUV in the supercar territory.\nThe all-new 7X debuts the Qianli Haohan G-ASD 4.1 driver assistance system, powered by 31 perception sensors, including standard LiDAR. The SUV also gets the Super Eva AI assistant alongside front-row zero-gravity seats with 12 massage points and eight massage modes.\nPhoto: Zeekr Cloud Comfort seats, with a 134-degree recline angle and 8.46 inches (215 millimeters) of power sliding travel, heating and pneumatic massage, are in the second row for luxury sedan-like comfort.\nRegardless of the trim, the X7 features a standard high-speed tire blowout stabilization system, which keeps the vehicle traveling straight and prevents rollovers or spins if a tire suddenly bursts at highway speed.\nAll trims also feature Continuously Controlled Damping (CCD) electromagnetic damping, the adaptive suspension technology that adjusts the firmness of a vehicle's shock absorbers in real time. The active road noise cancelation with laminated acoustic glass across all four doors is also on the menu.\nZeekr is selling the X7 in three distinct variants. The X7 RWD Max with the 75 kWh battery pack and 385 miles (620 kilometers) of range sits at the base of the lineup. Higher in the range is the RWD Max+ with the 85 kWh battery pack and 423 miles (680 kilometers) of range.\nPhoto: Zeekr This variant can also be ordered with the larger 103 kWh CATL Qilin battery, which takes the range all the way to 498 miles (802 kilometers). The same battery pack equips the AWD Ultra, but this variant can drive as far as 444 miles (715 kilometers) before it needs to be plugged in again.\nZeekr launched the all-new 7X with a promotional price starting at 216,800 yuan, which translates to roughly $32,400, instead of the usual 229,800 yuan ($34,300). The range-topping AWD Ultra is a 269,800-yuan ($40,300) deal.\nThe 2027 has already entered mass production, and the order book is open. Deliveries in China are expected to kick off immediately after the official unveiling. Customers in Australia and Europe will get their new X7s starting in December.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2027 Zeekr 7X Zeekr Zeekr SUV Guanghzou Auto Show 2026 Auto Guangzhou\nAbout the author: Elena Luchian\nElena started off as a sports reporter and five years later switched to automotive. How does that happen? Lots of writing, testdrives, traveling, off-road driving courses, track driving courses, defensive driving courses and diplomas. The diplomas might be \"useless\", but the knowledge she gained is priceless. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1969 Ford Torino GT SportsRoof Has a Numbers-Matching R-Code 428 Cobra Jet Ram Air and Other Goodies",
